body:
I agree this solution with macros is not pretty. Maybe I'll introduce additional macros that creates necessary variables, ie.:

```c
wrapper(creat, int, (const char * pathname, mode_t mode))
{
    expand_chroot_path_vars();
    debug("creat(\"%s\", 0%o)", pathname, mode);
    expand_chroot_path(pathname);
    return nextcall(creat)(pathname, mode);
}
```

I don't think it would improve readability if the hidden variables would be hidden even more. And there are at least two of them and not always both will be used, causing warnings, needing attributes to shut off the warnings etc etc. It might be better to give those hidden variables a very special and outstanding name, for example "special_tmpbuf" or something like that. Still non obviously hiding the fact that something like
```c
  p1 = expand...(path1);
  p2 = expand...(path2);
  useof(p1 and p2);
```
will fail badly.

Thak you to let me know :)
Just tested and seems like fts test still is failing.
